## Common mistakes

### Chat link appears in an inconsistent position

A homepage has a prominent link below the main heading:

<div style="background: #f3f2f1; padding: 15px; margin: 15px;">
  <h4>Homepage</h4>
  <p><a href="#">Chat to us</a> today!</p>
</div>
 
On other pages (but not the homepage), the "Chat to us" link only appears in the page footer.

<div style="background: #f3f2f1; padding: 15px; margin: 15px;">
  <h4>Footer menu</h4>
  <p><a href="#">Chat to us</a> <a href="#">Privacy</a> <a href="#">Cookies</a></p>
</div>
 
On every page that the "Chat to us" link appears, it needs to be in the same relative position (either below the main heading, or at the start of the footer).

## Related success criteria

Consistent Help is at level A but overlaps closely with the following level AA criteria:

* [3.2.3 Consistent Navigation (AA)](3.2.3.html) requires that repeated navigational elements (such as menu links) appear in the same relative order.
* [3.2.4 Consistent Identification (AA)](3.2.4.html) requires that repeated functionality has consistent labels. For example, the same link should not be labelled "Help" on one page and "Support" on another.
